d, well-fed laborers, not slaves. They had decades, thousands of workers, and an organized system—but the exact logistics remain uncertain. So, while we have strong *theories* and *clues*, we don't have a single, universally accepted *reconstruction* that accounts for every detail. That's what keeps the question alive—and part of the wonder.
